# A function of a block that applies itself as a widget: `fn @Tower n` whose block ends
# on `@Tower m` under a building `match` (Semantics ch. 4: a function defined in a block
# reads the block's names; ch. 8: a widget applied is transparent, and a widget that
# calls itself builds as deep as its data; ruling LS: a local function that calls itself
# has a signature; ruling TC: places are counted as built). Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests

@table: @unit
@table:
    !add <- Ui.Button($label=$"add")
    $count <- 0 then $count + 1 on !add
    @Tower: fn Nat -> @unit emit Ui.*
    fn @Tower n:
        Ui.Label($text=$"level {n} at {$count}")
        match n -? 1:
            ? m: @Tower m
            nil: Ui.Label($text=$"ground")
    @Tower 2
    Ui.Label($text=$"after")
